   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the output?\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">def update_hour():\n&nbsp;&nbsp;global new_hour\n&nbsp;&nbsp;new_hour = hour\n&nbsp;&nbsp;if is_dst:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;new_hour += 1\n&nbsp;&nbsp;else:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;new_hour -= 1\n\nis_dst = True\nhour = int(input(\"Enter hour: \"))\nupdate_hour()\nprint(\"New hour:\", new_hour)\n</pre>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1328724,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">New hour: 9</code>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "new_hour has the value 10 and can be accessed outside update_hour()."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328725,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">New hour: 10</code>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "The <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">global</code> keyword can be used to create a global variable from within a function. <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">new_hour</code> has global scope and can be accessed outside <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">update_hour()</code>."
    },
